Done. Commit `d1a58c92c` on `w4_id-ownership`.

**Acceptance**
| Criterion | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `cd cmd/bd && go test -run 'TestDaemonAutoStart' ./` | exit 0 → `builds/r2-step1.log` |
| `go test ./internal/importer/... ./internal/utils/... ./cmd/bd/...` (`BEADS_NO_DAEMON=1 BD_NO_DAEMON=true`) | exit 0, all six packages `ok` → `builds/r2-step2.log` |

**What changed, and one thing beyond the brief**

`cmd/bd/autostart_test.go`: new `isolateConfig(t)` helper; `TestDaemonAutoStart` calls it instead of a bare `config.Initialize()`. A plain `t.TempDir()` was not sufficient — config discovery falls back to `~/.config/bd/config.yaml`, which on this machine also carries w28's `auto-start-daemon: false` — so the helper writes an *empty* `.beads/config.yaml` in the temp dir to stop the search, then restores cwd and config on cleanup. No assertion and no repo config touched. No existing helper covered this.

`cmd/bd/claim_test.go`: `TestClaimExitCodesInDaemonMode` was failing for the same class of reason — it builds the child bd's environment from `os.Environ()`, so the `BD_NO_DAEMON=true` the Ship Gate itself exports leaked in and forced direct mode. It now pins `BD_NO_DAEMON=false` in the env it passes.

Beyond test files, one product fix I judged necessary: those two fixes uncovered `TestAutoFlushOnExit`, which fails about one run in three at HEAD with my test changes reverted. It is not a test bug. `MarkDirty` only queues its event on a buffered channel, so a mutation immediately followed by `Shutdown` — what `PersistentPostRun` does on every exit — leaves the run loop's `select` with two ready channels; when it takes shutdown first, `isDirty` is still false and the final flush is skipped, dropping the mutation. `cmd/bd/flush_manager.go` now drains queued `markDirty` events before deciding to flush, on both the `flushNow` and `shutdown` branches. 20 consecutive passes after, and the flush tests pass under `-race`. Flag if you would rather that race ship as a separate item.
